[{:db/id "q-325899/field-1/1f693f340afc78a910bc6fe5292af192790f366ee3028ce768556352a63b63e4" :answer/id #uuid "a4c4efd4-8696-5898-a4b3-798bdcb218e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sec(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325899/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8e7f442-f2af-5edb-81ed-98e3bbc10be6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325899/field-1/1f693f340afc78a910bc6fe5292af192790f366ee3028ce768556352a63b63e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-325899/field-1/1f693f340afc78a910bc6fe5292af192790f366ee3028ce768556352a63b63e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325899" :question/id #uuid "a6736c64-b952-51ed-a517-798f758cbddf" :question/math-academy-id "q-325899" :question/problem "Complete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola $16{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=64$ in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2} & =64 \\\\ \\frac{16{x}^{2}}{64}-\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{64} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have $a=\\sqrt{4}=2$ and $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-325899/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2669e657-da47-5e22-9ac5-7a69f3b0a55f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325899"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325896/f