uation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(1,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=1.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm 3x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{b}{1} & =3 \\\\ b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=1\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-325916/field-1" "q-325916/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32fc8440-e872-50e4-ab98-5861d1c7310e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325916"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325926/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "632913a9-9187-5044-8d6c-729a81a5b2ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325926/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d173244-2112-5a3d-9f87-a2db1e24abff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325926/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-325926/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325926/field-2/4770030a5b31b100afafcc5c6f2755c6cf14ec4c3e56fcf7c56d4ace77162137" :answer/id #uuid "e5e49199-0569-530d-8d96-4347ddf0e98c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}\\tan(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325926/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "98d90fa3-d556-5625-bfff-78d2a16e0840" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type