stions ["q-325926"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274725/field-1/b5d74ba0ee99b7cb150721737f422bae2310fb202031c82423aed37d398ad723" :answer/id #uuid "027dc694-71fd-5576-965e-8fe897d3290a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\sec(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274725/field-1/7763460aad7708831c85f861031e9236e41352d03525d18b1c3c52dbd23146e2" :answer/id #uuid "e1d55664-2fec-560d-86a0-d2ffb3f8e6fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sec(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274725/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3690e7d4-c802-5423-adbb-c82a4e70da0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274725/field-1/b5d74ba0ee99b7cb150721737f422bae2310fb202031c82423aed37d398ad723" :answer-field/choices ["q-274725/field-1/b5d74ba0ee99b7cb150721737f422bae2310fb202031c82423aed37d398ad723" "q-274725/field-1/7763460aad7708831c85f861031e9236e41352d03525d18b1c3c52dbd23146e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274725/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "59a4c35d-5135-5e1b-ac97-3ed9b9d66581" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274725/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "048ffd33-9d6e-5465-91ca-34315c778af1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274725/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-274725/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274725" :question/id #uuid "24d693f3-c81f-529f-ae93-8dafeedac4b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-274725" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/f81019b6a22b93d480be339eb2b58c642a2a01a098d0a74eb172c873ca254b09.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(\\sqrt{5},0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{5}} & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ b & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274725/field-1" "q-274725/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32fc8440-e872-50e4-ab98-5861d1c7310e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274725"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325927/field-1/3655764b6330814336036493cd14e5de40847b2f74f302e47a78a8ead2f39920" :answer/id #uuid "9628d248-208e-56c9-944f-e9eac8f9c3b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\sec(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325927/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "759de39f-b2cd-59e7-af40-484bd1d8006d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325927/field-1/3655764b6330814336036493cd14e5de40847b2f74f302e47a78a8ead2f39920" :answer-field/choices ["q-325927/field-1/3655764b6330814336036493cd14e5de40847b2f74f302e47a78a8ead2f39920"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325927/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "f5ac3534-c327-5568-b66f-a3a33718964d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325927/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f88f637-a2e4-5bdc-9efe-f14f5d46151e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325927/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-325927/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325927" :question/id #uuid "9a90e399-12c3-5736-af8a-cd387ebebbf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-325927" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/6a4ee1fd218118096dcdb2bd85b16477e2230b4634eb6c53e9fcab68f7d4939c.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(\\sqrt{6},0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{6}} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-325927/field-1" "q-325927/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32fc8440-e872-50e4-ab98-5861d1c7310e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325927"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106528/selection/4fbc3a5fb7ce8549fa8ac061d197c993e1e3d58e35ea158c1d34f50ca0a56559" :answer/id #uuid "ec576947-6dcd-5540-98a9-843867f605d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106528/selection/003b73d4bdba7c2fe17caeea2404a528c4b3002f6449328e5fbd16f559f49d7b" :answer/id #uuid "85a1ee1f-2f6d-5b6a-9644-ee729c86d8af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106528/selection/a02455aba649ec73757aefc7c5d526db91a0abb0b4d94e3d3b59b40a8eb556a1" :answer/id #uuid "66aec029-a516-5334-bac0-2b7aa90f0252" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106528/selection/1c6face4ba558a6a09526d67ba97a772d9429e3253d2cc8a0ff01621653884a6" :answer/id #uuid "50179e5b-61b5-5441-9de6-6c6babadf77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{3}}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106528/selection/7570289d3deca1415b3aa847876f6f2037f4ff0cef41594f676eb57c032ac82a" :answer/id #uuid "f83941c5-4a0e-5a65-b35f-9bdcc282a3ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106528/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ec1bf744-0b60-5665-b1c2-cea37072236d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106528/selection/4fbc3a5fb7ce8549fa8ac061d197c993e1e3d58e35ea158c1d34f50ca0a56559" :answer-field/choices ["q-106528/selection/4fbc3a5fb7ce8549fa8ac061d197c993e1e3d58e35ea158c1d34f50ca0a56559" "q-106528/selection/003b73d4bdba7c2fe17caeea2404a528c4b3002f6449328e5fbd16f559f49d7b" "q-106528/selection/a02455aba649ec73757aefc7c5d526db91a0abb0b4d94e3d3b59b40a8eb556a1" "q-106528/selection/1c6face4ba558a6a09526d67ba97a772d9429e3253d2cc8a0ff01621653884a6" "q-106528/selection/7570289d3deca1415b3aa847876f6f2037f4ff0cef41594f676eb57c032ac82a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106528" :question/id #uuid "f30b1e07-07d4-58c1-a237-16af51b64840" :question/math-academy-id "q-106528" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(5)^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{12} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficu