la (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/5516a6bbdb411a5f21bbf530ca93926c09f9fcfdb5d57a6947032d1525849560.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0]$ and $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the right branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the right branch are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-89350/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14527450-9b34-5982-9d87-b5a31870a70e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89350"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106598/selection/1be01a38655c9b80c5143f8e1af887b96d6afac0d8b99aa5a70070b461be0f30" :answer/id #uuid "8b7db0c5-d87c-5d5d-b02a-fe445ea7b111" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106598/selection/11ea745910ff697b9055ddbb7e7b8a23d1d92eec0a8c07053d7df7aa989d1cf5" :answer/id #uuid "deb32eb7-6f5b-5ebc-8b65-ceac2de901a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106598/selection/b99a41c2495bc5629f5e19e5dd0eb7719a9a673afa058fcedfb87312b0b99f96" :answer/id #uuid "bba4aa22-5c79-5a4a-b0e3-5a6ec79fc446" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/ensure 